"""
patch_L289_3_frame_hud.py -- interactive.html: the Sun's edge labels come
OUT; a camera-following triad, the Aries note, a grid-spacing chip and
per-axis grid colours go IN. Plotly's tick numbers return.

Tony's phone pass, 2026-09-05, on the first L-289 build: the twelve-edge
text labels shrank and vanished on zoom-out, were sliced at the box
boundary, and floated on nothing for edges beside the camera. His
design for the rebuild, settled the same evening:
- a TRIAD in the corner (x, y, z arrows) that turns with the camera,
  projected from the scene's camera and aspectratio after every move;
- the First Point of Aries glyph at the x tip; a tap opens a short note
  that this is the J2000 ecliptic frame, not a graph frame, with its
  source (NASA/JPL NAIF frames tutorial);
- one GRID CHIP naming the uniform spacing ("grid 0.2 AU"), updated when
  the frame zooms;
- grid lines coloured per axis to match the arrows.
The frame was VERIFIED before the note was written: feature_renderers.js
rotates IAU poles into the J2000 ecliptic by the mean obliquity; belts
are drawn in the ecliptic; the served index stores the Sun as
frame-origin. The HUD only reads the camera and redraws an SVG; it never
calls Plotly, so the 2026-09-02 click-deferral hazard does not apply.

Runs AFTER patch_L289_1 and patch_L289_2 (guards on the file at gallery
ae28621a). RUN: save at the GALLERY repo root next to interactive.html,
open in VS Code, Run. Then commit, push, report the SHA; Mode 5 on the
phone: rotate and watch the triad follow; tap the Aries glyph; +, -,
Home and watch the chip.

Guards on the LF-normalized md5 of interactive.html at gallery ae28621a;
CRLF working copies pass and are written back as CRLF. Refuses a second
run. All inserted text is ASCII (glyphs are HTML entities). No .bak.

Permanent: sunHud*, sunTriadUpdate, sunGridChipUpdate, SUN_AXIS_COLORS,
the .sun-hud/.sun-triad/.sun-grid-chip/.sun-frame-note styles and
markup. Removed: sunEdgeLabels*, SUN_EDGE_*. Disposable: this script.

Written September 5, 2026 with Anthropic's Claude Fable 5.1. Built on
gallery ae28621a8d8666f28978256c2b0b32854dc39ede at
https://github.com/tonylquintanilla/tonyquintanilla.github.io (main).
Ledger: L-289. Archive to documentation/ once run.
"""
